From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akashic <hoshiestar@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] ChunkBlockHashMap.get: with chunkmap.cache4Seguro, a
 non-server thread checks the coordinates of what the map returned

While the server thread puts a chunk in a new 16x16 block the Koloboke table grows, and an
unlocked get from another thread can return the block of another key. The map path returned
that chunk without checking (the 4-entry cache path checks). Now a chunk of another coordinate
becomes null for the outside reader. The false null for a loaded chunk in that window remains
and is documented as a known limit (chunkmap.md 12.4 item 3, 12.7).

Tests (TesteChunkmapCache4): swapped block (deterministic) and readers with the map growing.
Review finding I1 of Degrau B step 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ELhLZzamveLVoauHRY3hDN

diff --git a/src/main/java/thermos/wrapper/ChunkBlockHashMap.java b/src/main/java/thermos/wrapper/ChunkBlockHashMap.java
index ee615bcd..f3b5894c 100644
--- a/src/main/java/thermos/wrapper/ChunkBlockHashMap.java
+++ b/src/main/java/thermos/wrapper/ChunkBlockHashMap.java
@@ -184,14 +184,15 @@ public class ChunkBlockHashMap {
         Chunk[][] bunch = this.map.get((((long) (x >> 4)) << 32L) ^ (z >> 4));
         if (bunch == null) return null;
 
+        int hoshieX = x, hoshieZ = z; // Hoshiestar: a coordenada pedida, antes de o codigo original reduzir x e z (usada so pela parte 2, abaixo)
         x %= 16;
         z %= 16;
         Chunk ref = bunch[(x + (x >> 31)) ^ (x >> 31)][(z + (z >> 31)) ^ (z >> 31)];
 
         if (ref != null) {
-            // Hoshiestar start: H01 parte 2: com a chave ligada, so a thread do servidor grava o cache de 4 entradas; outra thread (ou thread do servidor ainda desconhecida) devolve o que achou no mapa sem gravar nada
+            // Hoshiestar start: H01 parte 2: com a chave ligada, so a thread do servidor grava o cache de 4 entradas; outra thread (ou thread do servidor ainda desconhecida) devolve o que achou no mapa sem gravar nada. Essa outra thread confere a coordenada do que achou: enquanto um put da thread do servidor faz a tabela do mapa Koloboke crescer, a consulta ao mapa pode devolver o bloco de 16x16 de OUTRA chave (a consulta sao duas leituras sem trava); chunk de outra coordenada vira null. O null falso para chunk carregado continua possivel nessa janela (src/docs/chunkmap.md, 12.4 e 12.7)
             if (HOSHIE_CACHE4 && Thread.currentThread() != hoshiestar.api.ThreadServidor.thread()) {
-                return ref;
+                return ref.xPosition == hoshieX && ref.zPosition == hoshieZ ? ref : null;
             }
             // Hoshiestar end
             last4 = last3;
